WEBVTT

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.260
According to the weather forecast,

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.640
due to radiative cooling or
a cold air mass or something,

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.600
this morning's temperature would
be as cold as the middle of winter.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:14.190
It wasn't until I started riding
my Cub that I noticed,

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:17.780
but when riding along like this,
I was able to feel the seasons

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.370
a lot more deeply than before.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.540
The air that day made it feel...
as though I were swimming in ice.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.670
"In Ice"
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 9"

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.670
The air that day made it feel...
as though I were swimming in ice.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.010
"In Ice"

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.010
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 9"

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:31.500
Ah... now that's warm.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.040
"2nd Year"

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.590
We have to do something.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:43.010
Something... Yeah, something.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.810
We really... might not have
any choice but to buy <i>those</i>.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.390
No, anything but <i>those</i>. They're so uncool.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:53.480
But I think it's our best option.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.400
Even so! There's no way I'm buying one.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:09.290
It's even starting to get
too cold for this, too.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:17.130
Ah... Your mess tin is cooking
your rice just fine, huh?

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.460
Mm-hmm.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:31.430
Excuse me... would it be okay...
if I ate with you?

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.480
Mm-hmm.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.670
Here. It's nice and hot.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.210
Thanks.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.630
Here, for you, too, Reiko-<i>chan</i>.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.170
Thanks.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.100
<i>Tè al latte.</i>

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:17.100
It's Italian milk tea. It's chilly today,
so I added a little grappa, too.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.690
"Caution: too much makes it
alcoholic and actionable"

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.690
It's Italian milk tea. It's chilly today,
so I added a little grappa, too.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.070
"Caution: too much makes it
alcoholic and actionable"

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.070
"Grappa"?

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:23.490
"Caution: too much makes it
alcoholic and actionable"

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:23.490
It's a brandy distilled from
leftover wine pomace.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.120
Stand up a minute.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.120
Huh?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.080
H-Hey...

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.550
Reiko-<i>chan</i>?

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.880
It's okay. You can fit.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:49.090
Shii-<i>chan</i>, if I stuff you into
the rear box of my Hunter Cub,

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:52.470
I can enjoy some hot coffee
or milk tea anytime.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:54.640
Huh?!

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:58.850
Actually, Shii-<i>chan</i>, are you okay
in just that coat all winter?

00:05:58.850 --> 00:05:59.690
Huh?

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.480
Even while you're riding your Moulton?

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:05.030
Mm-mm, I'm not that
cold wearing just this.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:06.700
Hmm...

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:10.870
Um, if you're cold, couldn't
you wear something more?

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.330
It's a struggle for me
to buy something else.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.160
This is all she has.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.330
I see...

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:24.420
I think I might have
something that can help!

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.220
I'm home!

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:33.100
Ah, welcome!

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.390
Hello.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:37.060
Wait here a minute.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.600
How would you like some
Mandheling high roast today?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.110
Oh... Yeah, that.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.860
Yes, please.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:53.200
Sorry to keep you.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.490
This is it.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.210
It kind of smells.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:05.920
Let me see that!

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:12.220
This is abrasive wool, isn't it? Amazing!
I've never seen the real thing before!

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.640
Ab-- What?

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:15.680
Abrasive wool.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:17.680
It's wool that has the bare
minimum washing done

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:21.020
after it is sheared from the sheep.

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:24.900
Hunters in the Rocky Mountains
and the cold regions of Canada

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:29.360
don't trust cold-weather gear with liners
that use anything other than this wool.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.240
The same with Burt Munro,
who rode the world's fastest Indian!

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:35.660
His racing suit wasn't made
from the latest materials;

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:39.000
he wore New Zealand wool
as he raced along the salt flats!

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.830
It doesn't seem suited to motorbikes.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:46.960
We can use this cardigan to make
a liner to fit under your jacket.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:50.800
And with the leftover wool, we can make
some stockings for you, Reiko-<i>chan</i>.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:52.470
I'd like that.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.260
Is that okay, Papa?

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:57.560
You've only worn it a few times
since I bought it for you.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:01.310
If you're going to wear it,
I'd be glad to let you have it.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.060
Reiko...

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:15.530
What do you think?

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.380
It's warm.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.060
I will take it.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:43.600
You have to add some oil
whenever you wash it.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:47.310
That means soaking it in hot water
with lanolin oil mixed in.

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.320
It's quite a bit of trouble.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.360
I can trust things that are trouble.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:59.910
I wasn't able to get much out of it,
but if it can find new life with you...

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:02.000
Thank you very much.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.620
Okay, start making it.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:04.500
Huh?

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:08.000
I was sure that <i>you</i>
would be able to sew it.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.380
You do your own maintenance
on your motorbike, and all.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:11.210
I can't.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.090
Huh? Papa?

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:17.140
No way, no way! About all
I can do is sew on buttons.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:19.430
And Mama can't even do that.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:26.980
Hmm?

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.650
Let's go to the school, right now.

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:37.700
Do you have an idea in mind?

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:41.290
If things go right, we may be
able to deal with this today.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:45.710
Well, we'd better hurry. Let's take care
of this before they close the front gate.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:48.080
Reiko-<i>chan</i>?

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.590
Does she have a helmet?

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:56.090
If the one that she used in middle school
will work, then there <i>is </i>that one.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:02.890
Here.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:04.140
Huh?

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.070
Huh?

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:20.620
You're fine, I tell you.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.580
Too fast!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.080
Turn a cardigan into a liner?

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:32.250
Also some stockings!

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.670
If we don't, we might freeze to death.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:40.300
I don't know about <i>that</i>. Why don't
you show me the material first?

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.760
This is it.

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:46.270
No way! Abrasive wool?!

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:49.560
If we can't make a liner out of it,
it might have to be thrown out.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:55.070
No, that would be a waste! Fine,
since my students' health depends on this,

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:56.940
I'll do it.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:05.540
--See you tomorrow!
--See you tomorrow!

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.090
There.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:17.760
Wow!

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:21.890
A zipper might hurt whatever you
wear under it, or even your skin,

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:24.220
so I went with buttons instead.

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:32.060
I used rubber buttons, like they use
on real rugby shirts, not the fake kind.

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.440
Oh, yeah?

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:36.020
And... here are the stockings.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:41.610
And also... Here, a thermos cozy.

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.780
Is that something you can use?

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:44.780
Yes!

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:47.370
If there's anything else
you need, just say so.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:50.660
I'll handle all of your woolen needs.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.460
--Thank you very much!
--Thank you very much!

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:45.970
Do you like your stockings?

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.810
Mm, they're pretty nice.

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:56.310
And how is your liner?

00:12:57.360 --> 00:13:02.610
Very good. I should be fine with
the cold for a while like this.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.590
Now for the weather forecast.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:22.970
Reports from the Kofu Local
Meteorological Office

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:26.640
say that Mt. Fuji has had its
first snowfall of the season.

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:30.470
According to the Meteorological
Agency's AMeDAS System...

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.290
The wool liner alone isn't enough anymore.

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:53.950
That's the thing about cold-weather gear.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:58.290
Once it gets colder than it can handle,
it just gives up on you.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:00.290
I don't think we can put off
buying <i>those </i>anymore.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:04.340
No way! They're so ugly!
I'm not putting one on my Hunter Cub!

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:06.760
But there's nothing else we can do now.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:09.800
--Good morning!
--I'm never buying one!

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:22.650
Are you heading out somewhere?

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:24.070
Just a little shopping.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:26.740
We still haven't decided to buy anything!

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:35.500
Please stop by the shop!
I'll have hot coffee waiting for you!

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.970
We really don't have any
choice but to install them--

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:59.480
No way. If it comes to putting
one of those on my Cub,

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:02.060
I'd rather keep it locked up
over the winter.

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:04.900
I don't really want to put one on, either.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:09.110
Even a used one is expensive,
and I can't buy a new one.

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:16.660
So warm...!

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:24.170
There it is.

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:28.090
A windshield.

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.680
Are you buying it?

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:38.640
"Super Cub Windshield"

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:42.230
Excuse me a second.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:46.780
"Checkout"

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:49.150
"Checkout"
Thank you very much.

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.450
Excuse me.

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:57.370
Do you have any more
windshields for a Super Cub?

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:00.750
Oh, we just sold our last one.

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:04.080
How about one that would fit a Hunter Cub?

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:08.670
Hmm... I don't see anything here.

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:13.180
Thank goodness. If they had one,
I might have lost my head and bought it.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:14.510
Me, too.

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:17.430
I would have thrown my money away
without thinking of the consequences.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:20.680
Oh, but one of our affiliates
has them in stock.

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.640
Would you like me to order them for you?

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.230
They should arrive here
in two or three days.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:36.120
Thank you for waiting.

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:41.000
Today I have cappuccinos for you.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.210
Mmm.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:48.840
It has that nice brandy aroma.

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:49.840
That's Uchida grappa,
made here in Yamanashi Prefecture.

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:51.840
"Caution: too much makes it
alcoholic and actionable"

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:51.840
That's Uchida grappa,
made here in Yamanashi Prefecture.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.880
"Caution: too much makes it
alcoholic and actionable"

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.880
You should add even more.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:55.930
"Caution: too much makes it
alcoholic and actionable"

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:55.930
I can't!

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:59.310
Just let me know when you need a refill.

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:00.890
Thanks.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:07.650
Are you going to put a windshield on?

00:17:07.650 --> 00:17:09.650
I already told you I wasn't.

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:12.530
They say it's the best way
to keep the cold away.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:15.820
So, does that mean you're putting one on?

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:18.950
My budget is awfully tight this month.

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:24.080
Um... if you're having trouble deciding,
couldn't you just try one on?

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.830
I actually got to use one of these
during the culture festival,

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:29.880
and that's when I decided to buy one.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:33.590
"Can I please ride one of your Cubs
with a windshield on it?"

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:37.800
We don't know anyone who would grant
such an opportunistic request.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:39.100
Yes, we do!

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:43.890
Come on!

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:45.730
Huh? Right now?

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:48.400
It'll be fine! Come on, hurry!

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.020
Thanks for the coffee!

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:56.150
Bye.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:04.830
See you later, Shii-<i>chan</i>.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:07.420
You'll be back again, won't you?

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:10.040
If this cold keeps up, we will.

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:21.760
I sure wish it would snow.

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:25.560
Mister!

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:27.440
Oh, what brings you here today?

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:29.940
Please, can I ride one of your Cubs?

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:31.400
Hmm?

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:36.530
All of my company bikes are out right now.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:40.450
All that's left here is this one.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:48.370
This one's been in an accident,
huh? The frame is bent.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:51.460
Yeah, it got hit by a truck.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:54.590
Apparently the oil cap got sent
flying when it went down.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:58.880
Now it leaks oil. I still let it
run for a while like that,

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:02.680
and now the head and cylinders are shot.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:04.060
It won't run?

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:09.190
A quick trip isn't a problem.
But it's noisy, and there's smoke.

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:12.440
Plus its power and top speed
are both way down.

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:15.480
Let me see the key.

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:49.180
--Thank you very much.
--Thank you very much.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:53.650
Well?

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:57.280
I've made up my mind.

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.490
You did say they were ugly.

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:04.950
If it works better, it's not ugly.
And <i>you </i>said you didn't have the money.

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:09.620
I can live on rice and retort pouches
until my scholarship money arrives.

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:11.000
Okay.

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:17.960
I have to say, while the windshield was
nice on that Cub, it was a real mess.

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:21.220
He said he was about to junk it.
Why don't you go ask him for it?

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:24.090
Only a fool would want that Cub.

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:34.150
So Cubs are really that good, huh?

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:22.570
Incredible.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:29.080
Incredible! Incredible! Incredible!

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:31.330
Yahoo!

00:21:40.710 --> 00:21:44.550
That day, we just kept on riding.

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:48.800
Maybe it was because we were
in such high spirits,

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:53.100
but after the sun went down and the
temperature fell, we both felt fine.

00:21:55.390 --> 00:21:59.440
We had done a number of things
to prepare for the cold.

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:05.110
We turned to a number of people for help.

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:07.950
I felt more comfortable around other
people than I had been before,

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:10.080
when it was for my Cub.

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:12.450
Thank you very much!

00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:19.130
In time, autumn would pass,
and winter would arrive.

00:22:19.130 --> 00:22:21.000
But...

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:25.300
I'm sure that with the bitter cold
of winter under control,

00:22:25.300 --> 00:22:30.010
it will no doubt feel great
and be enjoyable.

00:22:30.010 --> 00:22:31.970
After all...

00:22:31.970 --> 00:22:36.480
...our winterized Cubs, which we
thought would only restrain us,

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:41.480
were as promising and
full of potential as this.

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:22.830
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 10"
"Snow"

00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:25.920
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 10"
"Snow"
Episode 10: "Snow."
